## Conversation
Goal: serve moonshotai/Kimi-K3 on arm64 GB300 (sm_103) from self-built images.
K3's SiTU activation is unservable on public FlashInfer; the user found
flashinfer PR#4180 and asked to incorporate it; that PR proved unbuildable
(asserts SiTuGlu into an artifact that lacks it), and the working support was
instead reconstructed from the public vllm/vllm-openai:kimi-k3-arm64 image.

## Actions
Extracted the 31MB cubin-pool layer and the installed flashinfer package from
the public upstream image (registry API, anonymous token); diffed wheel vs
public v0.6.15.post1; ported the private-only delta as a patch; iterated a
JIT-compile falsification in a GB300 pod until the private module compiled,
loaded, and exported its *_private FFI symbols; added the pool-downloader
stage and the force-reinstall fix; validated end-to-end serving (correct
tokens, 40.3 tok/s AR, 165.2 tok/s with DSpark k=7).

## Errors & Mistakes
- r4 shipped a rediff of PR#4180 that CANNOT compile against the public
  artifact (unconditional SiTuGlu static_assert; "has no member SiTuGlu").
- r5 built the patched wheels and then pip skipped them: the vLLM wheel's
  requirements pre-installed stock flashinfer-python==0.6.15.post1 and
  "already satisfied" won at the same version string. Every image r1-r5
  shipped stock flashinfer; nothing noticed until a backend needed the patch.
- The agent-extracted patch missed three hunks that carry no private-looking
  token: module_name threading into gen_jit_spec (without it the AOT
  short-circuit loads the PUBLIC module -> AttributeError
  trtllm_bf16_moe_private), the lean-routing #endif closers ("unterminated
  #else"), and reduceTopKForLane in RoutingKernelTopK.cuh.
- FlashInferSetCubinCallback was invisible under -fvisibility=hidden until
  the wheel's cubin_loader.h (visibility("default") macro) was adopted.

## Dead Ends
- flashinfer PR#4180 as-is: red-CI draft; no published batched_gemm artifact
  (incl. the newer 17629de-61f1bc7) contains SiTuGlu. Revisit when NVIDIA
  publishes one.
- Installing upstream's arm64 wheels directly: flashinfer_jit_cache 0.6.15
  fails the startswith version check against post1 pins and drags ~490 lines
  of unrelated post-0.6.15 drift.
- marlin (correct but 2.9-7.3 tok/s) and triton (MXFP4 wrapper rejects SITU)
  as fast backends.

## Hints for Future Agents
- The pool is an OVERLAY, not a replacement: zero SwiGLU fused-act kernels,
  so never repoint ArtifactPath at it.
- The private module JIT-compiles at first MoE call (~4 min/node); prewarming
  it into the image is the known follow-up.
- vLLM kimi-k3 branch passes is_private=True unconditionally in
  trtllm_{mxfp4,nvfp4}_moe.py — this API is a hard requirement of the branch.
- MAX_JOBS defaults to 32; the AOT stage takes ~6h at that on a 128-CPU
  builder and 73 min at MAX_JOBS=128. sccache-as-ccbin does not cache nvcc
  device compiles, so this stage never gets faster from S3 cache.
- Full provenance and diffs: memory reference-k3-private-flashinfer-pool.

## Codebase Discoveries
_import_deep_gemm prefers site-packages over vllm.third_party (docstring says
so); the deepseek-ai wheel shadowed vLLM's vendored activation-aware copy,
which is why deep_gemm_mega_moe failed before the repin.

